    "b-day-scale-1": {
      "id": "b-day-scale-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "children": [],
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The run director's three capacity controls — worker pool, epoch ready queue, and tool/build slots — survive sandboxes intact; what changes is the mechanism behind the third and the resource the first is bounded by. Worker pool size remains the claim target and becomes a platform quota question, and compile pressure moves from shared-filesystem slot directories to orchestrator-owned admission plus per-sandbox vCPU."
        }
      ]
    },
    "b-day-scale-2": {
      "id": "b-day-scale-2",
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "kind": "decision",
        "title": "Decision (2026-08-13) — compile admission is orchestrator-owned",
        "tone": "success"
      },
      "children": [],
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Fleet-wide compile and tool admission is enforced by the orchestrator's global jobserver behind "
        },
        {
          "insert": "ORCH_GLOBAL_COMPILE_SLOTS",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", sized to sandbox vCPU. Per-epoch filesystem slot directories retire with the shared filesystem: on per-VM disks they are silently per-sandbox and enforce nothing fleet-wide."
        }
      ]
    },
    "b-day-scale-3": {
      "id": "b-day-scale-3",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "children": [],
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Sizing for 64 Concurrent Workers"
        }
      ]
    },
    "b-day-scale-4": {
      "id": "b-day-scale-4",
      "type": "structured-table",
      "props": {
        "columns": [
          "Per-sandbox",
          "64 sandboxes",
          "Tier"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "1 vCPU / 2 GiB / 4 GiB disk",
            "64 vCPU / 128 GiB / 256 GiB",
            "Tier 2 (100 vCPU) — fits but thin"
          ],
          [
            "2 vCPU / 4 GiB / 5 GiB disk — recommended",
            "128 vCPU / 256 GiB / 320 GiB",
            "Tier 3 (250 vCPU); Tier 2 suffices with stop-while-thinking, since only running sandboxes hold vCPU quota"
          ],
          [
            "4 vCPU / 8 GiB / 8 GiB disk",
            "256 vCPU / 512 GiB / 512 GiB",
            "Tier 4 or bring-your-own-compute"
          ]
        ]
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "b-day-scale-5": {
      "id": "b-day-scale-5",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "children": [],
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Two vCPU per sandbox matches the hot path — single-unit incremental compiles — with only the permuter wanting more cores; creation rate limits are a non-issue at 64, and bring-your-own-compute removes the quota ceiling past roughly 120."
        }
      ]
    },
    "b-day-scale-6": {
      "id": "b-day-scale-6",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "children": [],
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Stopped sandboxes hold disk quota until archived: 64 at 5 GiB is 320 GiB, just over Tier 2's 300 GiB, so either 4 GiB per sandbox or Tier 3."
        }
      ]
    },
    "b-day-scale-7": {
      "id": "b-day-scale-7",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "children": [],
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Idle Economics"
        }
      ]
    },
    "b-day-scale-8": {
      "id": "b-day-scale-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "children": [],
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "At roughly a quarter active duty cycle — minutes of model reasoning between tool-call bursts — the lifecycle strategy dominates the bill:"
        }
      ]
    },
    "b-day-scale-9": {
      "id": "b-day-scale-9",
      "type": "structured-table",
      "props": {
        "columns": [
          "Strategy",
          "Compute billed",
          "Added latency",
          "Verdict"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "Always running for the claim's lifetime",
            "128 vCPU continuously",
            "none",
            "pays roughly fourfold for idle"
          ],
          [
            "Stop while thinking",
            "~32 vCPU effective",
            "a wake of seconds after each long think",
            "adopted; see Lease, Claims, and Lifecycle"
          ],
          [
            "Fresh sandbox per tool call",
            "low idle, high churn",
            "boot, seed, and patch replay on every call",
            "rejected; loses workspace and incremental build state"
          ]
        ]
      },
      "children": []
    },
